# Semantic HTML and WCAG 2.1 AA

Target [WCAG 2.1](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/) Level A + AA. Prefer native HTML (and Mantine components that map to it) before ARIA. Capability tests stay in `web-feature-tests.mdc`; this rule is how markup is written. If video or audio is added, 1.2.x applies.

## Semantic HTML first (1.3.1, 4.1.2)

- Use native name, role, and value: `button`, `a`/`Link`/`Anchor`, labelled inputs, `table`, `h1`–`h6` via `Title order`, `header` / `nav` / `main` / `footer` / `section`.
- One `<main>` per page (`AppShell`). Name repeated `nav` (`aria-label="Main"`). Name `section`/`form` only when they are landmarks.
- Real headings in outline order. Do not fake headings with bold `Text` or `p`, or skip levels for style.
- `Button`/`button` for actions; `Link`/`Anchor` for navigation. Never `div`/`span` with `onClick` or `role="button"`.
- Lists: `ul`/`ol`/`li`. Data tables: Mantine `Table` with `Table.Th` headers.

## ARIA only when HTML cannot (4.1.2, 4.1.3, 2.5.3)

- First rule of ARIA: do not override native semantics (`role` on `button`/`h1`).
- `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby` for icon-only controls and unnamed landmarks. Visible text is the name otherwise; the accessible name must include that visible label.
- Status that does not take focus (toasts, in-flight rows): Mantine `notifications`, `Alert`, or `aria-busy` / live region. Do not put `role="alert"` on static copy.
- Never `aria-hidden` on a visible focusable control.

## Forms (1.3.1, 1.3.5, 3.3.1–3.3.3)

- Visible `label` on every input (`TextInput` / `NumberInput` / `Textarea` `label` prop). Placeholder is not a label.
- Required in the label (`withAsterisk`). Errors on the field (`error` / `aria-describedby`) with a fix suggestion when the format is wrong.
- Personal data fields get `autocomplete` (name, email, address) when those fields exist.

## Keyboard and focus (2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.4, 2.4.7, 2.5.2)

- All actions work with Tab / Enter / Space. No `onMouseDown`-only activation.
- Do not trap focus except in Mantine `Modal`. Do not `outline: none` without a 3:1 replacement (1.4.11).
- DOM order is the focus order. No positive `tabIndex`.
- Link text describes the destination (`Gardens`, not `Click here`).

## Perceivable (1.1.1, 1.4.1, 1.4.3, 1.4.11, 3.1.1)

- Keep `<html lang="en">` in `root.tsx`. Set `lang` on phrases in another language.
- Informative images: equivalent `alt`. Decorative: `alt=""` or CSS background. No filename or `image` alt.
- Color is not the only signal (pending, errors, required). Pair with text, icon, or `aria-busy`.
- Contrast via theme tokens (`theme.ts` / `--mantine-*` / `--color-text`): text 4.5:1 (large 3:1), UI and focus 3:1. No raw hex that drops contrast.

## Document (2.4.1, 2.4.2, 3.2.3)

- Descriptive page `title`. `AppShell` landmarks satisfy bypass-blocks; add a skip link only if repeated chrome has no landmarks.
- Repeated nav stays in the same order and uses the same names.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Prefer Mantine `Button`, `Title`, `Anchor`, `TextInput`, `Table`, `Alert`, `Modal`
- Label every control; keep heading order and one `main`
- Announce async status with notifications, `Alert`, or `aria-busy`

**Don't**

- Fake buttons, headings, or tables with `div`
- Use placeholder-only inputs or `outline: none` with no replacement
- Override native roles, or hide a focused control with `aria-hidden`

```tsx
<header>
  <nav aria-label="Main">
    <Anchor component={Link} to="/gardens">
      Gardens
    </Anchor>
  </nav>
</header>
<main>
  <Title order={1}>Gardens</Title>
  <TextInput label="Garden name" withAsterisk />
  <Button type="submit">Add garden</Button>
</main>
```

```tsx
// Bad — div-as-button; placeholder label; skipped heading; no focus ring
<div onClick={onAdd}>Add</div>
<input placeholder="Garden name" />
<Title order={3}>Gardens</Title>
```

```css
/* Bad */
button:focus {
  outline: none;
}
```
